35.3.6 Elfish racial ascension - elf selected as the race, did
  not weild a non-elven weapon (only elven dagger, elven short sword,
  elven broadsword, elven spear, or elven bow allowed), did not wear
  non-elven armor (only elven mithril, elven cloak, elven leather
  helm, elven shield, and elven boots allowed).
  Patience: Slight  Luck: Slight  Planning: Trivial

Elfie Notes

Elves: Elves have most of the armor types available (lacking only
a shirt and gloves). Plus, their armor is rather good. Elves also
have a variety of weapons, also rather good. (Plus two artifact
weapons that are pretty close to useless.) It is true that an elf
can make a fine wizard. But, I am trying to do all of races and do
them in unique classes. I already chose to do an orc wizard. This
puts the elf in a bit of an awkward spot. Why? well, because if an
elf is not going to wear any armor or weild any weapon that does
not have "elven" in the name (or description) and is not a
wizard, they will not be able to get magic resistance.

(OK, to be technical, I suppose that the elf could change
alignment to Neutral or Lawful and wish for one of the artifacts
that grant MR by carrying, but that seems out of the spirit of
this stupid trick.)

So, can I do an ascension without MR? I don't know. I'll be more
than a bit scared of touches of death. I would really like to see
all L's genocided before the Castle. I suppose I could keep some
potions of hallucination on hand for when Rodney shows up. I think
that the plan will be this: Choose Ranger as the class for the elf.
Rangers are good at killing things at a distance which is good
as I won't have any heavy-hitting artifact melee weapons. Wishes
(if/when I get that far) will go getting some heavy-hitting pets
(ie. tricked out Archons. Or possibly Alexes or Trolls) and
genocides to eliminate troublesome monsters (the touch-o-death
dealers that are geocidable - only L's, and ones that can cause
problems for pets - t's, purple worms, green slimes).

Even if I manage to maintain careful play with this game it
sounds dicy.

